{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Of David. YHWH is my light and my salvation—whom shall I fear?</b> Some say:" "My light — in the night, when there is no light, for the soul fears." "And my salvation — in the day. And others say:" "My light — pertains to the matters of the soul." "And my salvation — to the matters of the body." "And the stronghold of my life — binds the soul to the body; therefore he will not fear a man who would separate them."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:43.002796017Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}